{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791588899,"nonce":"0tHJcklCbuvmtTR8isBrmcklgI8=","message":"Inset box shadows are drawn as of 64dc3af.\n\n**Change**: PaintShadow has `inset?: boolean` in TypeScript and in the addon. setPaint splits a shadow list into RenderProps.shadow and RenderProps.inner_shadow, each kept in CSS order, so one `box-shadow` value can mix outer and inset layers. The host's `box-shadow` reader accepts `inset` instead of reporting it. A drop-shadow filter refuses an inset layer. The `shadow-inner` token and its utility now draw. The docs describe inset layers.\n\n**Test** (tests/native-theme.mjs, offscreen):\n- An inset shadow darkens the inside edge and leaves the centre white.\n- Nothing is drawn outside the box, and the rounded corner clips it.\n- Outer and inset layers in one value both draw.\n- `shadow-inner` darkens the top edge.\n- Removing the shadows leaves the geometry identical.\n- Under the Hybrid shape (n = 1.3334237337112427) the inset layer's corner changes with the fill.\n\n**Found in blinc_abi, not changed here**: an outer shadow with zero blur is not drawn. `0 0 0 8px green` paints only stray square corners behind the box, and `8px 0 0 green` paints nothing. Blurred outer shadows draw correctly. The earlier shape test now uses a blurred outer shadow, so it checks a drawn shadow.","files":null}]}